text	activeStatusCollectionVarDefText	cora	{"name": "text", "children": [{"name": "recordInfo", "children": [{"name": "id", "value": "activeStatusCollectionVarDefText"}, {"name": "dataDivider", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "system"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "cora"}]}, {"name": "type", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "recordType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "text"}]}, {"name": "validationType", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "validationType"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "textSystemOne"}]}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "12345"}]}, {"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2017-11-01T17:51:58.000000Z"}], "repeatId": "0"}, {"name": "updated", "children": [{"name": "updatedBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "141414"}]}, {"name": "tsUpdated", "value": "2023-03-02T15:30:04.115694Z"}], "repeatId": "1"}, {"name": "createdBy", "children": [{"name": "linkedRecordType", "value": "user"}, {"name": "linkedRecordId", "value": "12345"}]}, {"name": "tsCreated", "value": "2017-10-01T00:00:00.000000Z"}]}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "Status för aktiv, bestämmer om den entitet där den används är aktiv eller inaktiv. En inaktiv entitet är närmast jämförbar med att den är raderad, d.v.s. den räknas inte med i något läge. En viktig skillnad från att ta bort entiteten är att andra entiteter kan upprätthålla relationen till den, om man i ett senare läge vill aktivera den igen."}], "attributes": {"lang": "sv", "type": "default"}}, {"name": "textPart", "children": [{"name": "text", "value": "Status for active, decides if the entity where it is used is active or inactive. An inactive entity is closest comparable to a removed entity i.e. it is not taken into account in any situation. An important difference from a removed entity is that other entities may retain their relationship to the inactive entity, if the entity later will be reactivated. "}], "attributes": {"lang": "en", "type": "alternative"}}]}
